Hi Chris,

Thanks for providing this resource, it has helped a bunch with troubleshooting and learning ctmm. I've got a couple of my own questions that I've tried to solve and getting no joy, hoping it is a quick fix!

1. When creating AKDE's and then plotting them, I'm consistently getting the following warning messages:

> plot(bevtel,UD=BevUD)
Warning messages:
1: In CI.UD(x, max(level.UD), max(level), P = TRUE) :
  Outer contour extends beyond raster.
2: In CI.UD(x[[i]], l, level, P = TRUE) :
  Outer contour extends beyond raster.

I've attached images of the plots that give this warning, and the strange contours that result. In other packages I would insert my own grid so that I could be certain the HR would fall inside the extent, do you have any suggestions here?

2. When writing UDs as shapefiles, they maintain the XY projection units determined in as.telemetry. For me this goes from long: 152.xxx and lat -27.yyy to x=2.67 and y=-0.475, seemingly a division by approx 57.  Trying to project this onto a habitat map in ArcGIS is then problematic. Again, any suggestions on how I could work around this?

Thanks in advance,

Anthony

